.TH MDT.EXPORTS.CLEAR 4 2026-09-08 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
mdt.exports.clear, obdfilter.exports.clear \- clear per-NID export statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param mdt." FSNAME "*.exports.clear=" VALUE
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param obdfilter." FSNAME "*.exports.clear=" VALUE
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per MDT and OST device.
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writing any value to
.B exports.clear
resets
.BI exports. NID .stats
for every NID that has exports on the device.
The LDLM counters in
.BI exports. NID .ldlm_stats
are not reset.
.PP
Since release 2.18.0, it also immediately frees the statistics of every idle
NID (one with no exports left), however long it has been idle.
The background scan controlled by
.BR nid_stats_idle_time (4)
only frees entries that have been idle for longer than that timeout.
.PP
The value written is not otherwise interpreted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Clear the NID statistics on every MDT of the
.B testfs
filesystem:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl set_param mdt.testfs-*.exports.clear=1"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B mdt.exports.clear
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 1.8.0.
.\" Added in commit 1.6.0-1131-g0521288fde
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdt.nid_stats_idle_time (4),
.BR lustre (7),
.BR lctl (8)
